---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell hero-copy">
      <div class="release"><span>Private beta</span><a href="/features/">See what works today →</a></div>
      <h1>C++ development,<br />on your iPad.</h1>
      <div class="hero-bottom">
        <p class="lead">cppMax compiles and runs real arm64 programs on your iPhone or iPad. Your projects stay on the device. No remote build machine required.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button blue" href="/support/#beta-access">Get beta access</a><a class="button light" href="/how-it-works/">How can this run on iOS?</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="shell hero-shot">
      <div class="shot-label"><span>01</span><span>Editor, project files, and console</span><span>Illustrative beta UI</span></div>
      <img src="/images/editor-ipad-placeholder.svg" alt="Illustration of the cppMax editor, file browser, and console on an iPad" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="today section">
    <div class="shell today-grid">
      <div class="sticky-copy"><p class="eyebrow">The beta today</p><h2>Enough IDE to build something useful.</h2><p>The beta is not pretending to be Xcode on a smaller screen. It has the parts needed for a real edit, build, and run loop, with clear limits.</p><a class="text-link" href="/features/">Read the full beta checklist</a></div>
      <div class="capabilities">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Write across a project</h3><p>Open several files in tabs. Move through the file tree. Use basic C++ highlighting and static analysis.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Build with Clang</h3><p>The bundled LLVM, Clang, and LLD toolchain produces a real arm64 ELF. Most CMake projects work.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Debug the first mile</h3><p>Set basic breakpoints and inspect console output through <code>std::iostream</code>.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Keep the project in Git</h3><p>Clone, commit, branch, and work with remote repositories without leaving cppMax.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-section section rule">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="work-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">One job, start to finish</p><h2>Make a tool on the train. Run it before your stop.</h2></div><p>Imagine a small parser that reads local log files and writes a report. The whole loop stays on the iPad.</p></div>
      <div class="work-grid">
        <figure class="product-figure blue-figure"><img src="/images/git-files-placeholder.svg" alt="Illustration of project files and Git controls in cppMax" /><figcaption><span>Project view</span><span>Replace with final app screenshot</span></figcaption></figure>
        <div class="work-steps">
          <article><span>1</span><div><h3>Clone or start fresh</h3><p>Pull an existing Git project or create a local folder.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>2</span><div><h3>Edit and build</h3><p>CMake configures the project. Clang and LLD create the executable.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>3</span><div><h3>Sign the ELF</h3><p>The beta signs builds automatically. After beta, one envToken is planned for a standard program.</p></div></article>
          <article><span>4</span><div><h3>Run it again offline</h3><p>The signature follows the ELF's SHA-256 hash. An unchanged build can run as often as you need.</p></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="privacy-section">
    <div class="shell privacy-grid">
      <div class="privacy-copy"><p class="eyebrow">Local means local</p><h2>Your source does not need a round trip through somebody else's server.</h2><p>cppMax edits, compiles, signs, and runs on the device. Network access is optional for Git remotes, beta support, and the planned ad option for envTokens.</p><a class="text-link light-link" href="/privacy/">Read the privacy summary</a></div>
      <div class="local-diagram" aria-label="Diagram showing the cppMax toolchain running locally"><div class="device-name">Your iPad</div><div class="pipeline"><span>Source</span><b>↓</b><span>Clang + LLD</span><b>↓</b><span>arm64 ELF</span><b>↓</b><span>cppMax runtime</span></div><div class="no-cloud">No compiler server</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="runtime-section section">
    <div class="shell runtime-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Why it can run</p><h2>iOS does not execute the ELF. cppMax does.</h2><p class="lead">The app includes a custom AArch64 interpreter. A small virtual Linux layer translates its supported system calls into iOS operations.</p><p>That distinction matters. You get a real compiler output and programs that can work with local files, while cppMax stays inside the execution model Apple allows.</p><a class="text-link" href="/how-it-works/">Open the technical explanation</a></div>
      <figure class="product-figure acid-figure"><img src="/images/runtime-placeholder.svg" alt="Illustration of a local cppMax build and runtime log" /><figcaption><span>Build and run output</span><span>Illustrative beta UI</span></figcaption></figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="roadmap section rule">
    <div class="shell roadmap-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Honest beta status</p><h2>Stable enough to test. Still missing pieces.</h2></div>
      <div class="status-list">
        <div><span class="status live">In beta</span><p>Local files, arm64 compilation, ELF execution, Git, most of CMake, console I/O, and basic breakpoints.</p></div>
        <div><span class="status limited">Limited</span><p>The virtual Linux layer covers roughly 50 system calls. Highlighting, analysis, and debugging are still basic.</p></div>
        <div><span class="status planned">Planned for v1</span><p>OpenGL translation, phone-as-keyboard pairing, deeper IDE tools, and interface customization.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sm"><div class="shell cta-band"><div><p class="eyebrow">Private beta</p><h2>Try cppMax before the App Store release.</h2></div><a class="button" href="/support/#beta-access">Beta access details</a></div></section>
</Layout>
<style>
  .hero { padding: 82px 0 0; }
  .hero-copy h1 { margin-bottom: 50px; }
  .release { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; margin-bottom: 46px; padding-bottom: 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); font: 700 .69rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .release span { color: var(--orange); } .release a { color: var(--blue); text-decoration: none; }
  .hero-bottom { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr; align-items: end; gap: 50px; margin-bottom: 72px; }
  .hero-bottom p { margin: 0; }
  .hero-bottom .actions { justify-content: flex-end; margin: 0; }
  .hero-shot { position: relative; }
  .hero-shot img { width: 100%; border: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .shot-label, figcaption { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; padding: 11px 0; color: #6f6e67; font: 650 .63rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .today-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; gap: 100px; }
  .sticky-copy { position: sticky; top: 116px; align-self: start; }
  .sticky-copy p:not(.eyebrow) { max-width: 470px; }
  .capabilities article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 70px 1fr; padding: 32px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .capabilities article:first-child { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .capabilities article > span { grid-row: span 2; color: var(--blue); font: 700 .72rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .capabilities h3 { margin-bottom: 8px; font-size: 1.55rem; }
  .capabilities p { margin: 0; }
  .capabilities code { color: var(--blue); }
  .work-section { background: var(--paper-2); }
  .work-heading { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.3fr .7fr; align-items: end; gap: 70px; margin-bottom: 58px; }
  .work-heading h2 { margin: 0; max-width: 820px; }
  .work-heading > p { margin: 0; }
  .work-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.12fr .88fr; gap: 46px; align-items: start; }
  .product-figure { margin: 0; }
  .product-figure img { width: 100%; border: 1px solid rgba(23,23,20,.25); }
  .blue-figure figcaption { color: #354eae; }
  .work-steps { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .work-steps article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 46px 1fr; padding: 25px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .work-steps article > span { color: var(--blue); font: 700 .73rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; }
  .work-steps p { margin: 0; }
  .privacy-section { padding: 110px 0; color: white; background: var(--blue); }
  .privacy-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; gap: 110px; align-items: center; }
  .privacy-section h2 { max-width: 780px; }
  .privacy-section p { color: #dce3ff; }
  .privacy-section .eyebrow { color: var(--acid); }
  .light-link { color: white; }
  .local-diagram { padding: 26px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.35); }
  .device-name, .no-cloud { padding: 14px; font: 700 .7rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .device-name { color: var(--ink); background: var(--acid); }
  .pipeline { display: flex; align-items: center; flex-direction: column; padding: 24px; border-inline: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.25); }
  .pipeline span { width: 100%; padding: 16px; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3); text-align: center; }
  .pipeline b { padding: 7px; color: var(--acid); font-weight: 400; }
  .no-cloud { border: 1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,.42); color: #bfc9f7; text-align: center; text-decoration: line-through; }
  .runtime-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: 70px; align-items: center; }
  .runtime-grid h2 { font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 5.2rem); }
  .acid-figure figcaption { color: #596e2e; }
  .roadmap-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 90px; }
  .status-list { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .status-list > div { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 145px 1fr; gap: 20px; padding: 24px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .status-list p { margin: 0; }
  .status { justify-self: start; padding: 6px 8px; border-radius: 3px; font: 700 .63rem/1 ui-monospace, monospace; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .live { color: #17622f; background: #cdf0d6; } .limited { color: #8d402c; background: #ffd8ce; } .planned { color: #3349a4; background: #dce3ff; }
  .cta-band .eyebrow { color: var(--acid); }
  @media (max-width: 850px) { .hero-bottom, .today-grid, .work-heading, .work-grid, .privacy-grid, .runtime-grid, .roadmap-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 42px; } .hero-bottom .actions { justify-content: flex-start; } .sticky-copy { position: static; } }
  @media (max-width: 540px) { .release { gap: 20px; } .release a { text-align: right; } .shot-label span:last-child, figcaption span:last-child { display: none; } .status-list > div { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
